course: dictionary
lesson: 10176
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word tier is a good example. «The wedding cake had three tiers, each one smaller than the last.» Here a tier is one layer of the cake, placed on top of another.
explain: Read the words around the word for more clues. «The fans sat in the top tier of the stadium, high above the pitch.» Here a tier is a row or level of seats. «He hoped to reach the top tier of the league.» Here a tier is a level in a ranking.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does "the top layer of the stadium" fit? Yes, so tier means a level. A tier can be a layer you can see, or a level in a system you cannot see.
fact: A tier is one of several layers or levels placed one above another.
fact: A tier can also be a level in a system or ranking, such as the top tier of football.
fact: «Tiers» means more than one layer or level.
fact: Old English «dēor» meant any wild animal, like German «Tier» (animal) today; it later narrowed to one kind of animal, the deer.
fact: English tier is a different word from German Tier, so a look-alike word does not give you its meaning.
exercise: «The wedding cake had three tiers.» What is a tier here? | A candle on top | A knife for cutting cake | A kind of sweet icing | *A layer of the cake, one above another
exercise: «He hoped to move up to the top tier of the league.» What does tier mean here? | *A level in a ranking | A type of cake | A tyre on a car | A row of seats in a stadium
exercise: «The stacked cups had 4 in the bottom tier and 1 on the top.» How many cups were in the bottom tier? | 3 | 1 | *4 | 2
test: «The theatre had tiers of seats rising up the back wall.» What does tier mean here? | *Rows or levels of seats, one above another | Ticket prices | A kind of cake | Stage lights
test: Maya says tier means a car tyre. Is she right? | Not sure, so she should skip it | Yes, a tier is a wheel on a car | Yes, tier and tyre are spelled the same | *No, tier means a layer or level, and tyre is a different word
exam: Which sentence uses tier to mean a layer or level? | «The tier was very kind to the dog.» | *«The cake had five tiers, one on top of another.» | «She ate a tier for lunch.» | «The tier barked at the cat.»
